ason-at-cincinnati</guid><category>Women's Soccer</category><description><![CDATA[<img alt="Alexis Pashales battles against a defender during a match at Dick Dlesk Soccer Stadium in Morgantown." src="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&image_path=/images/2026/11/4/ex1_106.jpg" /><br /><br />CINCINNATI, Ohio – The West Virginia University women's soccer team prepares for its regular-season finale at Cincinnati on Thursday, Nov. 5. Kickoff at Gettler Stadium in Cincinnati, Ohio, is set for 7 p.m. ET.]]></description><media:thumbnail url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_system&amp;image_path=/images/2026/11/4/ex1_106.jpg" /><media:content url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&amp;image_path=/images/2026/11/4/ex1_106.jpg"><media:title>Alexis Pashales battles against a defender during a match at Dick Dlesk Soccer Stadium in Morgantown.</media:title></media:content><enclosure url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&amp;image_path=/images/2026/11/4/ex1_106.jpg" length="1" type="image/jpg" /><pubDate>Wed, 4 Nov 2026 13:02:00 EST</pubDate><s:sport_id>13</s:sport_id><s:story_id>59638</s:story_id></item><item><title>WVU to Face No. 13 Texas Tech in Rare 9:30 Kickoff Time on Saturday Night</title><link>https://wvusports.com/news/2026/11/4/football-wvu-to-face-no-13-texas-tech-in-rare-9-30-kickoff-time-on-saturday-night</link><guid>https://wvusports.com/news/2026/11/4/football-wvu-to-face-no-13-texas-tech-in-rare-9-30-kickoff-time-on-saturday-night</guid><category>Football</category><description><![CDATA[<img alt="West Virginia coach Rich Rodriguez visits with reporters in the Milan Puskar Center on Tuesday, Nov. 2, 2026." src="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&image_path=/images/2026/11/4/Rodriguez11326-Main.jpg" /><br /><br />MORGANTOWN, W.Va. – The most treacherous portion of West Virginia University's football season begins Saturday night in Lubbock, Texas, when the Mountaineers face 13th-ranked Texas Tech, coming off an impressive 34-26 victory over then-22nd ranked Arizona last Saturday.]]></description><media:thumbnail url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_system&amp;image_path=/images/2026/11/4/Rodriguez11326-Main.jpg" /><media:content url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&amp;image_path=/images/2026/11/4/Rodriguez11326-Main.jpg"><media:title>West Virginia coach Rich Rodriguez visits with reporters in the Milan Puskar Center on Tuesday, Nov. 2, 2026.</media:title></media:content><enclosure url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&amp;image_path=/images/2026/11/4/Rodriguez11326-Main.jpg" length="1" type="image/jpg" /><pubDate>Wed, 4 Nov 2026 12:00:00 EST</pubDate><s:sport_id>2</s:sport_id><s:story_id>59636</s:story_id></item><item><title>Mountaineers Defeat James Madison to Claim Sun Belt Conference Title</title><link>https://wvusports.com/news/2026/11/3/mens-soccer-mountaineers-defeat-james-madison-to-claim-sun-belt-conference-title</link><guid>https://wvusports.com/news/2026/11/3/mens-soccer-mountaineers-defeat-james-madison-to-claim-sun-belt-conference-title</guid><category>Men's Soccer</category><description><![CDATA[<img alt="Harry Hogben in action for WVU men's soccer against James Madison" src="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&image_path=/images/2026/11/3/110326_West_Virginia_79.JPG" /><br /><br />HARRISONBURG, Va. (Nov. 3, 2026) – The No. 9 West Virginia University men's soccer team defeated James Madison, 2-0, Tuesday evening at Sentara Park. With the victory, the Mountaineers claimed a share of the Sun Belt regular-season championship.]]></description><media:thumbnail url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_system&amp;image_path=/images/2026/11/3/110326_West_Virginia_79.JPG" /><media:content url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&amp;image_path=/images/2026/11/3/110326_West_Virginia_79.JPG"><media:title>Harry Hogben in action for WVU men's soccer against James Madison</media:title></media:content><enclosure url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&amp;image_path=/images/2026/11/3/110326_West_Virginia_79.JPG" length="1" type="image/jpg" /><pubDate>Tue, 3 Nov 2026 22:23:00 EST</pubDate><s:sport_id>6</s:sport_id><s:story_id>59635</s:story_id></item><item><title>Cooke’s Career Night Lifts West Virginia to Win Over Rhode Island</title><link>https://wvusports.com/news/2026/11/3/womens-basketball-cookes-career-night-lifts-west-virginia-to-win-over-rhode-island</link><guid>https://wvusports.com/news/2026/11/3/womens-basketball-cookes-career-night-lifts-west-virginia-to-win-over-rhode-island</guid><category>Women's Basketball</category><description><![CDATA[<img alt="Gia Cooke defends a Rhode Island player in the Mountaineers season opening win" src="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&image_path=/images/2026/11/3/BBD00405.JPG" /><br /><br />MORGANTOWN, W.Va. – The West Virginia University women's basketball team opened the regular season with a narrow 68-64 win over Rhode Island on Tuesday evening inside Hope Coliseum in Morgantown.]]></description><media:thumbnail url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_system&amp;image_path=/images/2026/11/3/BBD00405.JPG" /><media:content url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&amp;image_path=/images/2026/11/3/BBD00405.JPG"><media:title>Gia Cooke defends a Rhode Island player in the Mountaineers season opening win</media:title></media:content><enclosure url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_